            <ArticleTitle>Prinzmetal's angina during cyclophosphamide therapy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1155-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The first case of cyclophosphamide-induced myocardial ischaemia with electrocardiographically documented ST-segment elevation, T-wave inversion, arrhythmias, angina pectoris and cardiac decompensation is reported. The data suggest that cyclophosphamides induces myocardial ischaemia by eliciting coronary artery spasm.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
